    "updated_at": "2019-05-03T09:55:50Z",
    "body": "To create an inactive document, you need to navigate it. If you then go back in history and the document wasn't evicted from the \"bfcache\" (salvageable wasn't set, in HTML terms), it'll be active once more. At this point this might only be testable in Firefox (and maybe Safari), but Chrome plans to add this too.\r\n\r\nTo suspend a worker you make its owner document inactive.\r\n\r\nThis is the theory, how well all of this works in practice these days I'm not very sure of, as it's not tested to great extent.",
